02:08:54.500 --> 02:08:56.600
We learned about the different datatypes.

02:08:56.600 --> 02:08:59.900
We also learned how to update and delete data.

02:08:59.900 --> 02:09:04.200
And we learned how to query 
and select data from the database, right?

02:09:04.200 --> 02:09:07.100
So, we learned a lot of the core concepts in SQL.

02:09:07.100 --> 02:09:09.800
And up to this point, if you guys 
have been following along, 

02:09:09.800 --> 02:09:12.200
then you have a pretty good 
fundamental understanding 

02:09:12.200 --> 02:09:14.500
of the different things 
that we can do in SQL.

02:09:14.500 --> 02:09:17.800
Now, obviously we didn’t cover everything, 
but we covered a lot of the basics, right?

02:09:17.800 --> 02:09:21.500
And we've been using this student table 
which just has three columns.

02:09:21.500 --> 02:09:23.100
One primary key.

02:09:23.100 --> 02:09:26.000
And, you know, we learned how to create this table.

02:09:26.000 --> 02:09:27.600
We learned how to insert all this information.

02:09:27.600 --> 02:09:30.300
We learned how to update and delete.

02:09:30.300 --> 02:09:33.400
And then also just, you know, 
query for the specific language.

02:09:33.400 --> 02:09:37.400
Here’s a problem though, 
is this is a very simple example, right?

02:09:37.400 --> 02:09:42.500
I mean it’s one database table 
